WEBVTT

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.810
You cannot run from us, the
 Nubatama ninja forces-degozaru.

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.240
You are like a rat trapped 
in a maze-degozaru...

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.380
Next will be your final attack.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.960
I would act only after careful thought.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:01.970
Ninja Master Withdraws

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.870
Please!

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.200
Elaine...

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.970
It’s a good card, but not 
useful for attacking.

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:29.210
So in the end, as I figured,

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:30.710
this is my only hope!

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:35.380
Enter the fray! I ride the 
ruler of all knights...

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.030
The King of Knights, Alfred!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.400
Oh? Alfred, is it-degozaru?

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:52.590
The king of the Royal Paladins, who gains 
power based on the number of his loyal allies.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:56.230
I am impressed that you still have a 
card of this caliber remaining-degozaru.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.740
That’s Aichi’s trump card.

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:03.890
Making sure to have his grade 3 left... 
It looks like my tutelage has born fruit.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:10.620
Alfred’s skill is that, for each Royal 
Paladin as a rear-guard, he gains 2000 power.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.290
That means, maximum, he gets +10000 power.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:17.630
When you add in his own power, that means it 
is possible to attack with a maximum of 20000.

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:21.310
On the other hand, my 
Voidmaster’s power is 9000.

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:26.250
Even if I guard with a shield of 
10000, that’s only 19000 total.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.740
It would not be enough to defend 
against the attack-degozaru.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.470
However!

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:33.570
You only have three Royal 
Paladins in your rear-guard.

00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:38.110
Your precious Alfred’s skill 
only gives him +6000-degozaru.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.950
Perhaps you think to add 
another two units-degozaru,

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.640
but with your hand so small, 
that’s not an option-degozaru.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:45.210
That’s not true.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:49.950
Royal Paladins can call upon their 
allies without any your hand.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:51.820
They are bound to one another by trust!

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:52.740
What?!

00:03:52.740 --> 00:03:54.420
First, I move Marron to the back.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.390
And then I activate Barcgal 
and Alfred’s skills!

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.490
Flogal!

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.390
Knight of Silence, Gallatin!

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.890
Now there are five Royal Paladins!

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:22.900
They had that sort of skill-degozaru?

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.660
Yes! These are my Royal Paladin Knights!

00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:31.410
Fine then. Show me the power of your Knights!

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.450
I attack Voidmaster with 
Gallatin, boosted by Flogal!

00:04:42.500 --> 00:04:43.300
Again?

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:45.980
Ninja Art: Body Replacement 
Technique-degozaru?!

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.100
Oh, don’t you start with the -degozaru, too!

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:54.860
That level of attack isn’t 
going to faze me-degozaru!

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.320
Then, next...

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.950
I attack with Alfred!

00:05:06.520 --> 00:05:08.430
Power 20000-degozaru?

00:05:08.430 --> 00:05:10.330
I have no choice but to take this-degozaru.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.790
Twin Drive!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:19.940
First check...

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.500
Second check...

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:28.010
Stand trigger, activated!

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.010
What the...

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:31.730
I give Gallatin +5000 power!

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.710
Plus, I stand the Gallatin 
which had just attacked!

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:42.970
Great going, Brother!

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.930
That makes 5 damage!

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.240
Only 1 more!

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:47.360
OM, yo!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.620
I attack with Gallatin, boosted by Marron!

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:56.630
Ninja Art: Body Replacement 
Technique-degozaru!

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:00.710
This won’t be enough-degozaru...

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.610
Go forth, all of you!

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:06.360
Protect Voidmaster at all costs-degozaru!

00:06:12.230 --> 00:06:14.220
I managed to get through that-degozaru...

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.720
What’s wrong?

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.880
He should have just let 
that attack go through.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:23.790
I see!

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:26.150
Since he used Intercepts,

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:30.950
that means the final card in that ninja’s 
hand isn’t one he can guard with.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.600
Almost certainly.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.680
Which means that the only way to 
defend against Aichi’s next attack

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:38.410
will be if he draws a heal trigger.

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:44.350
So you’re saying it would have been better to 
just bet on a heal trigger in the first place.

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.300
Exactly.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.690
If he had drawn a heal trigger, he 
could not only reduce his damage by 1,

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:51.300
but also give +5000 power to a card.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:57.680
And with that extra power, he’d be able to 
guard the next attack by using less cards.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.720
In other words, he could 
maintain the size of his hand.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.810
If he isn’t capable of such basic strategy,

00:07:04.010 --> 00:07:06.440
this fight is over.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:09.960
I attack Voidmaster with the 
Gallatin I just stood up!

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:19.450
Is that really Sendou?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:21.910
How would you survive?

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.980
Aichi Sendou!

00:07:23.980 --> 00:07:26.090
I-I...

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.150
I would make sure I always had 
a line of retreat behind me.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.720
That weak-willed boy, who always 
thought about running away...

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:38.070
He’s not just standing his 
ground, he’s fighting bravely!

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.900
He drew a trigger

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:42.120
to lead his way to victory...

00:07:42.550 --> 00:07:44.050
Now, what will you do?

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:46.160
Will you guard, or not?

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.790
I check for a damage trigger-degozaru...

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:53.280
No trigger.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:07:57.310
Alas-degozaru.

00:07:57.930 --> 00:08:00.250
Winner: Aichi Sendou!

00:08:06.880 --> 00:08:08.000
I did it!

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.120
Great going, Brother!

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.610
Great, man! What a comeback!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.600
Thanks...

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:16.110
I’d expect nothing less 
from someone who beat me!

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:17.870
Oh, get off your high horse.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:20.820
Well, look at you.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.750
Just as you said.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:28.060
You sure have improved, Aichi!

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.530
You’ve taken all I’ve taught you to heart!

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:33.530
Whatever you say, Lose-umi!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.620
I see.

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:37.570
It looks like he’s met a lot of new friends.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:43.700
But man, I can’t believe you beat a ninja!

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.790
Uh, he calls himself a ninja, 
but that’s actually...

00:08:46.790 --> 00:08:47.710
Huh?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:49.390
He’s gone!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.750
Oh, no!

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.400
W-What’s wrong?

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.970
I totally wanted to get 
that ninja’s autograph!

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.920
Right... He’s a ninja, so I should have figured 
he’d disappear into the shadows without a sound...

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.520
Damn it! I let my guard down!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:09.880
What would you do with that 
guy’s signature anyway?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.560
What would I do? It’d be so cool!

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.910
Hey! If it isn’t Sendou!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:17.850
M-Mr. Mark?

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:20.220
Morikawa and Izaki as well!

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:23.500
Are you all participating in this tournament?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:28.280
Yeah! He just fought with a ninja, and won!

00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:31.010
Oh! Ninja! Fantastic!

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.390
I sure wish I could have seen that!

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.470
Anyway, what are you doing here, Teach?

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.220
Uh, isn’t it obvious?

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:44.810
I heard there was a card game tournament, and I 
couldn’t keep my blood from boiling and joining in!

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.600
Joining in?

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.600
Oh yeah! You love cards too, don’t you? Teach.

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.460
Yes! They are my favorite!

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:54.960
Ooh! You’ve got a great 
teacher, Brother Aichi!

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:55.670
Yup!

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:58.820
Um, Mr. Mark...

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.870
What’s in the bag?

00:10:01.790 --> 00:10:05.000
T-This? Nothing important.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.660
It’s definitely not a ninja costume!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.830
Now then, let’s start the next fight!

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:13.990
Um, could you please put 
this in the locker room?

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:20.000
Mr. Mark, thank you for the good fight.

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:21.410
-degozaru.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:27.340
We will now begin the 3rd and 
4th fights of the 2nd Round!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.100
Stand up!

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:31.020
Vanguard!

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:47.580
Attack, Asura Kaiser!

00:10:47.580 --> 00:10:49.580
Finish Hold!

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:51.040
Damn it...

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.790
Winner, Kamui Katsuragi!

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:55.900
All right!

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.810
Super Kool, Kamui the great!

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.370
SK, yo!

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:00.470
But of course!

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:04.690
You think I, the great Kamui Katsuragi, 
would lose in the 2nd Round of a Shop Tournament?

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.170
As expected from Kamui...

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:11.370
That little shrimp’s not cute at all...

00:11:11.370 --> 00:11:13.870
The shop girl’s having a tough fight...

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.400
Both of them have 4 damage...

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:21.360
And they both have the 
same number of units out.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.160
See? It’s pretty close.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:27.550
Pretty close? Well, I guess 
that’s how it seems at a glance.

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:28.660
But...

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:30.370
Amaterasu’s Soul Charge.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:35.630
First, I check the top card of my deck.

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:37.630
Silent Tom, huh?

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:40.640
I’ll put this one on the bottom of my deck.

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.800
And then I call...

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.930
Oracle Guardian, Hermes.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:48.350
His eye can predict the 
future, and see through all.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:52.580
Until this turn is over, 
you must reveal your hand.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:53.310
What?

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:55.610
That’s Hermes’s skill.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.770
Come on now, hurry up.

00:11:57.650 --> 00:11:59.680
But...

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:01.820
Brigitte and Tristan?

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:03.590
And your deck too, if you please.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:05.530
That too?!

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:07.680
Sorry, but that’s the way this card works.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:14.420
Leave that one on the top.

00:12:14.420 --> 00:12:17.380
I attack Stardrive Dragon with Hermes!

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:19.800
I guard with Tristan!

00:12:29.510 --> 00:12:33.390
Next, I boost with Cocoa, 
and attack with Silent Tom!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:41.560
Brigitte’s shield is 0, so she can’t guard!

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:43.680
So, she attacked because she knew that?

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:45.110
That’s playing dirty.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.660
That’s not all!

00:12:47.180 --> 00:12:49.050
Check for a damage trigger.

00:12:49.050 --> 00:12:50.370
No trigger, right?

00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:57.570
She checked her deck before, so 
she knew which card she’d draw!

00:12:57.570 --> 00:12:59.460
Man, how unfair can you get?!

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.960
But that’s the way Misaki plays.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:06.220
I attack with Amaterasu, boosted by Gemini.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:12.090
Twin Drive check...

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.080
Milk...

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.700
Wiseman... No triggers.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:19.670
But my power is 22000.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:24.070
Even if you activate a damage trigger, 
the highest shield you can have is 15000.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:27.560
In other words, you cannot 
defend against this attack.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:33.540
The only chance left to you 
is to draw a heal trigger.

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.160
Damage check...

00:13:37.660 --> 00:13:39.490
No trigger...

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:45.300
Winner: Misaki Tokura!

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:58.000
We have now decided upon the four people 
who get to enter the tournament finals!

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:02.190
The winner of A block, Aichi Sendou!

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:04.400
Attaboy, Aichi!

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:05.940
The brightest star of the small fry!

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:06.900
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:10.180
The winner of B block: Misaki Tokura!

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:11.130
She’s blushing!

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:12.640
How cute!

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:14.450
Shut up!

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:17.380
W-Why are you getting angry at me?!

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.280
The winner of C block: Kamui Katsuragi!

00:14:20.280 --> 00:14:22.570
The Great Kamui, best in Japan!

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:24.100
No, no... The best in the world!

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.360
BW, yo!

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:27.060
TB, yo!

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:28.660
DB, you know?

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:33.020
Say what?! Callin’ me a total 
bonehead and a damn brat?!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.000
The winner of D block: Toshiki Kai!

00:14:40.250 --> 00:14:44.320
And so these four will be entering 
the tournament finals. However...

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:45.300
Before that...

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:46.800
We draw the tournament brackets, right?!

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.830
No, we take a lunch break.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:52.220
W-What?!

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:55.090
See? It’s written right here.

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:58.330
First Round, Second Round
Lunch Break
Semi-Final Round, Final Round

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.920
Oh, look at that!

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:00.510
Therefore,

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:04.910
we’ll resume at 1 PM, 
so please don’t be late.

00:15:05.310 --> 00:15:08.910
Phew, it’s sure hard being the referee.

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:11.010
My back’s killing me...

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.850
There’s still an hour left.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:19.280
What am I supposed to do with 
all this pent-up excitement?!

00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:22.200
It’s noon, so why not eat lunch?

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.140
But I didn’t bring anything...

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:25.380
I did!

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:26.660
E-Emi?

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:29.910
Here, Aichi, your lunch.

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:31.880
Lunch?

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:33.200
You made it for me, Emi?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.030
You made it yourself, Miss Emi?

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.530
You’re so amazing, Miss Emi!

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:43.950
Well, Mom helped me a little bit.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:49.590
Actually, Mom made most of it.

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.530
What? What are you trying to say?

00:15:58.230 --> 00:16:02.280
Actually, I can understand 
a little cat language.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:03.260
Really?

00:16:03.260 --> 00:16:05.440
No... I was just joking.

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:08.380
Masaki just...

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.910
...made a joke?

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:16.530
Uh, I think he’s saying that you can’t 
eat your lunch inside the store.

00:16:16.530 --> 00:16:18.410
Oh, is that true?

00:16:18.760 --> 00:16:21.910
Yeah. No food or drink allowed.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:25.720
Y-You realize how bad it’d be 
to get the cards dirty, right?

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.120
I see...

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:30.180
I’m sorry. I didn’t know.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:35.610
But what should we do about the lunch?

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:38.290
Well, there is a bench 
by the side of the shop.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:39.230
Okay!

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.850
I didn’t know that Card Capital 
had a place like this.

00:16:43.630 --> 00:16:46.560
It’s not really that relaxing, but it’s fun!

00:16:47.510 --> 00:16:48.480
Tea?

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.120
Oh, thank you.

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.070
Sorry about kicking you out.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:55.950
Oh, it’s fine. Eating lunch out here is fun.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.180
Is it? That’s good to hear.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:01.530
The cat also has an exit?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.130
Yes, a cat-door.

00:17:04.030 --> 00:17:05.410
Fascinating!

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:06.490
Really?

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:07.750
I guess so.

00:17:11.230 --> 00:17:13.330
My goddess’s lunch!

00:17:13.330 --> 00:17:14.990
MGL, yo!

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:17.510
It sure looks yummy...

00:17:19.430 --> 00:17:21.970
My goddess’s lunch!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.320
We’ll have a fun picnic today!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:34.660
Dear, let’s have lunch over there!

00:17:34.660 --> 00:17:37.070
Yes, let’s, Emi!

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:42.750
I made sandwiches.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.980
Ooh, you’re so good at cooking, Emi!

00:17:46.970 --> 00:17:48.370
Here, Dear!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:53.180
Is it good?

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.730
Yes! So delicious!

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:03.770
Just you wait! One day, for sure I’m gonna...

00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:06.700
Are you really sure I can have some?

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:09.110
Thanks a gazillion! TG, yo!

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:11.640
It’s fine.

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.470
What the...?!

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:16.620
What are you two doing?

00:18:16.620 --> 00:18:20.120
She said that she made plenty, 
and asked if we wanted some.

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.910
How about you, Kamui?

00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:24.490
You fools!

00:18:24.490 --> 00:18:29.170
You guys aren’t worthy enough
 to eat my goddess’s lunch!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:30.110
Hey!

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:35.880
I’m free to give the lunch 
<i>I</i> made to anyone <i>I</i> want!

00:18:36.180 --> 00:18:39.130
Uh, sure, right...

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:42.220
Emi, please don’t be angry.

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.600
Let’s all eat together, Kamui.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:47.490
Are you sure, Brother?

00:18:47.490 --> 00:18:49.820
Fine. There’s plenty to go around.

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:52.110
I suppose I can let you 
eat my lunch, at least.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.650
Here, have a bite of my lunch!

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:00.230
Say "ah"!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:03.210
Ah!

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:07.260
Miss Emi, are you serious?

00:19:07.260 --> 00:19:09.520
Huh? Uh, sure...

00:19:09.520 --> 00:19:14.160
Finally! Finally my feelings 
have gotten through to Miss Emi!

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:18.850
W-Well then, don’t mind if I do.

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:20.560
Ah!

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:24.480
Oh! I think he wants us to do this.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:27.570
Ah!

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:28.850
Ah!

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.720
Ah!

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.200
Delicious! Miss Emi,

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:37.320
it’s so... So very...

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.320
Kamui the Lame!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.650
KL, yo!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:44.910
What do you think of the tournament?

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:46.550
I expected better.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:47.860
Really?

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:53.000
There’s the shop girl who just barely had 
her first fight in the tournament finals!

00:19:53.220 --> 00:19:55.650
What a shocker!

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:58.030
It’s only because the 
competition was so pitiful.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:20:00.970
Then, how about Aichi?

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:06.270
He came all this way just so that 
he could fight you, you know.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:07.830
What do you plan on doing?

00:20:08.230 --> 00:20:09.560
It’s irrelevant.

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.310
No matter who my opponent 
is, or what their goal is,

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:14.850
I will defeat anyone who challenges me.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.900
That’s the kind of Vanguard Fighter I am.

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:21.450
Sure, you say stuff like that. But 
you’re actually having fun, right?

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:22.500
What?

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.410
Oh, nothing!

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.270
Thanks for waiting!

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.410
We will now draw the brackets 
for the tournament finals!

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:38.170
There are slips of paper with the 
numbers 1 through 4 inside this box.

00:20:38.490 --> 00:20:43.520
Each of the 4 fighters will draw 
one to decide their positions.

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:46.300
Now, we’ll start with Aichi.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:48.540
Here.

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:50.680
Right.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:56.140
Hold on, don’t open it yet.

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:58.340
We’ll have you all open them at once.

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.980
R-Right...

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:01.980
Next, go on, Kai.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.960
And the final one.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:10.990
Save the vests for cats!

00:21:11.230 --> 00:21:12.330
Huh?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.750
Vests for cats?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.380
Close! He meant "best for last", I bet.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:21.090
Now, it’s finally time to open them up!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:25.840
This might decide if I have 
a match against Kai...

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:28.680
Now, go on!

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:36.880
One!

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:37.780
Four.

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:40.020
One and four?

00:21:40.350 --> 00:21:42.320
Not Kai, again...

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:44.740
I’m three.

00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:46.750
Which means...

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:49.160
My opponent will be you, Brother.

00:21:50.060 --> 00:21:53.640
I have to beat Kamui to fight Kai.

00:21:54.970 --> 00:21:59.040
I’m not going to hold back, even 
if you’re my opponent, Brother!

00:22:01.290 --> 00:22:03.500
Right! I wouldn’t have it any other way!

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:10.970
Card Capital Shop Tournament Semi-Finals...

00:22:11.380 --> 00:22:13.300
Both simultaneously...

00:22:13.570 --> 00:22:14.940
Begin!

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:54.360
All right! I managed to win my 
fight against the Ninja Master!

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:55.880
Good going, Brother!

00:23:55.880 --> 00:23:57.830
You’ve gotten plenty strong, Brother!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:59.530
Please, fight with that confidence!

00:23:59.530 --> 00:24:00.790
No matter who you’re up against.

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:02.110
Right. Thanks.

00:24:02.110 --> 00:24:04.060
Wait, then I’m fighting you next, Kamui?

00:24:04.060 --> 00:24:06.070
All right! Here it comes!

00:24:06.070 --> 00:24:09.420
In that case, my brother yesterday 
will be my brother today!

00:24:09.420 --> 00:24:11.830
Together we will fight fair and square!

00:24:11.830 --> 00:24:12.690
Understood.

00:24:12.690 --> 00:24:14.770
Next time: Aichi vs. Kamui

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:18.380
Picture it... If I beat Kamui, 
then Kai will be next!
